---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "About Us – Bulk HEIC to JPG Converter";
const description =
	"Learn about BulkHEICtoJPGConverter.com — a fast, private, and free batch HEIC to JPG converter that runs entirely in your browser.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
		<p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">About</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
			Why we built this
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			HEIC is a brilliant format — iPhone photos take up about half the space
			of the equivalent JPG. But that brilliance falls apart the moment you
			need to send, upload, or open those photos on a Windows PC, an Android
			phone, or any website that doesn't understand HEIC.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			We kept running into that exact wall: a dozen iPhone photos that refused
			to upload to a form, email, or old photo editor. Every "free" online
			converter we found was either painfully slow, limited to a few files,
			or — worse — uploaded our private photos to some server.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			So we built the tool we wished existed: a <strong>batch</strong> HEIC to
			JPG converter that is <strong>fast</strong>, <strong>free</strong>,
			<strong>unlimited</strong>, and <strong>100% private</strong> — because
			every conversion happens locally, on your own device. Nothing is ever
			uploaded.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
			We hope it saves you as much time and frustration as it saved us.
		</p>

		<div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 p-5 text-center dark:border-zinc-800">
				<p class="text-2xl font-semibold">0</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">uploads. Ever.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 p-5 text-center dark:border-zinc-800">
				<p class="text-2xl font-semibold">∞</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">file limit</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 p-5 text-center dark:border-zinc-800">
				<p class="text-2xl font-semibold">$0</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">free, forever</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>